1
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
They were "Strange Fruit". Some called them the greatest rock band of the '70s. They haven't
played together for 20 years. No wonder they're worried about their performance.

2
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Still Crazy is a comedy, music film directed by Brian Gibson.

3
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
In the 1970s, Strange Fruit were it.

4
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:30,000
They lived the rock lifestyle to the max, groupies, drugs, internal
tension and an ex front man dead from an overdose.

5
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Even their demise was glamorous; when lightning struck
the stage during an outdoor festival.

6
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Twenty years on, these former rock gods they have now sunk deep into obscurity when the idea of a
reunion tour is lodged in the head of Tony, former keyboard player of the Fruits.

7
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Tony sets out to find his former bandmates with the help of former manager Karen to see
if they can recapture the magic and give themselves a second chance.

8
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Tony Costello, played by Stephen Rea.

9
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Hughie, played by Billy Connolly.

10
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Les Wickes, played by Jimmy Nail.

11
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:42,000
David "Beano" Baggot, played by Timothy Spall.

12
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Ray Simms, played by Bill Nighy.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
Karen Knowles, played by Juliet Aubrey.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
Still Crazy is a 1998 British comedy film directed by Brian
Gibson (his final film before his death in 2004).

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
The plot concerns a fictional 1970s rock band named Strange Fruit, who,  two decades after splitting up, are persuaded
to get back together to perform at a reunion in the same concert venue where they played their last gig.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
The film focuses on the personal lives of the band members and those closest to them, their
individual experiences with approaching middle-age and the success that eluded them.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
It was nominated for two Golden Globes in 1999 in two categories: Best
Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy and Best Original Song.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
The film explores themes of manager, birthday, 1970s, bus, stage.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
